and that the pedestrian faced when it stepped onto it: dev.position ('location of the device head') ahead of kin.position along kin.heading ('direction the body points') within a cone and a reach. dev.position is not used as a stop line or crossing."},{"span":"t","atoms":["dev.pedestrian_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'illuminated and steady' is the head's state dont_walk_steady."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a pedestrian' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian."},{"span":"e1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane","st.sidewalk","dev.pedestrian_signal","dev.governs","dev.position","kin.position","kin.heading"],"derived":[],"source_spans":["ref2"],"justification":"Entering the highway lawfully pursuant to subparagraph (1) or (2) borrows their words: (1) 'While the “Walk” indication or walking person symbol is illuminated, pedestrians facing the signal may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal'; (2) 'While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated, is flashing and is accompanied by a countdown timer, a pedestrian may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal'. It is the pedestrian's latest step from a sidewalk (st.sidewalk) onto the roadway or lane r (rel.occupies of st.roadway / st.lane) made while the head d (dev.pedestrian_signal) governing r (dev.governs) showed walk, or dont_walk_flashing with its countdown, and the pedestrian faced d (dev.position ahead of kin.position along kin.heading within the cone and reach)."},{"span":"e2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"Continuing to cross is the pedestrian's footprint still overlapping r (rel.occupies) while d shows the steady indication."},{"span":"ob2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane","kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"Proceeding to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone or other place of safety is moving off the roadway or lane crossed: while the footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies), the pedestrian moves (kin.speed, 'magnitude of velocity'), at the pace the standard bounds. kin.speed is used as the magnitude of motion, not as acceleration."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"st","standard":"as soon as possible","concepts":["kin.speed"],"params":["p.pedestrian_clearing_speed_min"],"convention":"pedestrian clearance walking speed: a pedestrian still on the roadway after the steady indication proceeds as soon as possible where its speed is at least a floor well below the slow walking speed the clearance interval is timed for; lingering or halting on the roadway is below it","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"r","rule":"NRS_484B_287_1c","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"NRS_484B_287_1d","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"NRS_484B_287_1e","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_060_A","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_060_B","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_140_B_o2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_46_030_o1","map":{"subject":"v"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_46_030_o2","map":{"subject":"v"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"ref2","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-283-1d1","quote":"While the “Walk” indication or walking person symbol is illuminated, pedestrians facing the signal may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal"},{"span":"ref2","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-283-1d2","quote":"While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated, is flashing and is accompanied by a countdown timer, a pedestrian may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian), not engaged by NRS_484B_287_1c, NRS_484B_287_1d, NRS_484B_287_1e, LVMC_11_30_060_A, LVMC_11_30_060_B, LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1 or LVMC_11_30_140_B_o2, with no vehicle v of the scene engaged by LVMC_11_46_030_o1 or LVMC_11_46_030_o2. There are a pedestrian head d (dev.pedestrian_signal) showing dont_walk_steady and a roadway or lane r governed by d (dev.governs) such that the subject's footprint overlaps r here and the subject's latest step from a sidewalk onto r (history bound: that step, searched back without other limit) was made while d showed walk, or dont_walk_flashing with its countdown, and the subject faced d. The subject faces d where, with Δ the vector from its kin.position to d's dev.position and h its kin.heading: h·Δ > 0, (h·Δ)² ≥ p.ped_signal_facing_cos² · (Δx² + Δy²), and Δx² + Δy² ≤ p.ped_signal_facing_reach². Where that step lies before the recording, applicability is unknown.","obligation":"The subject's speed (kin.speed) is at least p.pedestrian_clearing_speed_min: it keeps moving off the roadway rather than lingering on it.","params":["p.pedestrian_clearing_speed_min","p.ped_signal_facing_cos","p.ped_signal_facing_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"ob2","why":"'proceed to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone ... or other place of safety' is read through the pedestrian's motion while still on the roadway; the direction it moves in (forward or back to the curb it left) is not read, and the kind of place reached is not checked.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"st","why":"'as soon as possible' is read as a speed floor at every observation on the roadway after the steady indication; the pedestrian's own ability (a slower walker) is not measured.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The pedestrian stepped onto r from the sidewalk facing d while d showed walk; d now shows dont_walk_steady and the pedestrian stands still (0.0 m/s) in the middle of r."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the pedestrian walks on across r at 1.3 m/s."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"d shows dont_walk_steady and the pedestrian waits on the sidewalk, off r."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Same as forbid but the pedestrian's speed is not observed.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The recording begins with the pedestrian standing on r while d shows dont_walk_steady; its step onto r is not recorded, so whether it entered lawfully cannot be told.","boundary":"the pedestrian's step from the sidewalk onto r, which lies before the recording"}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.pedestrian_clearing_speed_min","unit":"m/s","value":0.5,"convention":"the speed below which a pedestrian still on the roadway counts as lingering rather than proceeding to a place of safety: about half the 3.0 ft/s (0.9 m/s) walking speed to which pedestrian clearance intervals are timed for slower pedestrians","source":"MUTCD section 4E.06 pedestrian clearance walking speeds (3.5 ft/s, 3.0 ft/s for slower pedestrians)"},{"name":"p.ped_signal_facing_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.87,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about thirty degrees) between a pedestrian's heading and the line from its position to a pedestrian signal head at which the pedestrian counts as facing that head: the lateral offset of a far-side head from the crossing's line plus a pedestrian's heading wander","source":"MUTCD section 4E.08 (pedestrian signal heads placed at the far end of the crossing, in the pedestrian's line of sight)"},{"name":"p.ped_signal_facing_reach","unit":"m","value":40.0,"convention":"the largest distance from a pedestrian to a pedestrian signal head at which the head counts as the one across the crossing the pedestrian faces: a wide urban crossing (six lanes and a median, about 30 m) plus the head's set-back behind the far curb","source":"MUTCD section 4E.08; AASHTO Green Book urban cross-section widths"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}

