 and that the pedestrian faces: dev.position ('location of the device head') ahead of kin.position along kin.heading ('direction the body points') within a cone and a reach. dev.position is not used as a stop line or crossing."},{"span":"t","atoms":["dev.pedestrian_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'illuminated and steady' is the head's state dont_walk_steady."},{"span":"s1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a pedestrian' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian."},{"span":"ob1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"Proceeding to cross the highway is coming onto the roadway or lane the head governs: the pedestrian's footprint comes to overlap it (rel.occupies of st.roadway / st.lane). The highway (DEF-NRS-484A-095) includes the sidewalk, but the sibling words 'must proceed to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone' place the sidewalk outside the crossing, so the crossing begins on the roadway."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a pedestrian' (the one excepted) is the same admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian."},{"span":"e1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane","st.sidewalk","dev.pedestrian_signal","dev.governs","dev.position","kin.position","kin.heading"],"derived":[],"source_spans":["ref2"],"justification":"Entering the highway lawfully pursuant to subparagraph (1) or (2) borrows their words: (1) 'While the “Walk” indication or walking person symbol is illuminated, pedestrians facing the signal may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal'; (2) 'While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated, is flashing and is accompanied by a countdown timer, a pedestrian may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal'. It is the pedestrian's latest step from a sidewalk (st.sidewalk) onto a roadway or lane (rel.occupies of st.