re are a pedestrian head d (dev.pedestrian_signal) showing dont_walk_flashing without its countdown attribute and a roadway or lane r governed by d (dev.governs), the subject faces d, and the subject's footprint did not overlap r at the previous observation. The subject faces d where, with Δ the vector from its kin.position to d's dev.position and h its kin.heading: h·Δ > 0, (h·Δ)² ≥ p.ped_signal_facing_cos² · (Δx² + Δy²), and Δx² + Δy² ≤ p.ped_signal_facing_reach². Excepted: the subject is continuing a crossing it began lawfully under subparagraph (1) — its latest step from a sidewalk onto a roadway or lane was made while a pedestrian head governing that roadway or lane showed walk and the subject faced that head, and its footprint has overlapped no sidewalk since.","obligation":"The subject's footprint does not overlap r at this observation: it has not proceeded onto the roadway.","params":["p.ped_signal_facing_cos","p.ped_signal_facing_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"ob1","why":"'proceed to cross the highway' is read as the pedestrian's footprint coming onto the roadway or lane the faced head governs; walking on the sidewalk is not crossing.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"c0","why":"the signal that indicates to a pedestrian is read as a pedestrian head that governs the roadway or lane to be crossed and that the pedestrian faces within a cone and a reach.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"e2","why":"'continue to cross' is read as not having returned to a sidewalk since the lawful entry.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"At the curb, the pedestrian faces a head 15 m away across roadway r that governs r and shows dont_walk_flashing without countdown; at the next observation its footprint overlaps r."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same head and state; the pedestrian waits on the sidewalk and its footprint never overlaps r."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The faced head shows walk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The pedestrian steps onto r facing the head, but the head's state is not observed.","masked":["dev.pedestrian_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The pedestrian stepped onto the first roadway from the sidewalk while the head governing it showed walk, reached the median, and now steps onto the second roadway r while its faced head shows dont_walk_flashing without countdown: it is continuing a lawful crossing."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.ped_signal_facing_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.87,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about thirty degrees) between a pedestrian's heading and the line from its position to a pedestrian signal head at which the pedestrian counts as facing that head: the lateral offset of a far-side head from the crossing's line plus a pedestrian's heading wander","source":"MUTCD section 4E.08 (pedestrian signal heads placed at the far end of the crossing, in the pedestrian's line of sight)"},{"name":"p.ped_signal_facing_reach","unit":"m","value":40.0,"convention":"the largest distance from a pedestrian to a pedestrian signal head at which the head counts as the one across the crossing the pedestrian faces: a wide urban crossing (six lanes and a median, about 30 m) plus the head's set-back behind the far curb","source":"MUTCD section 4E.08; AASHTO Green Book urban cross-section widths"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
