{"node_id":"NRS_484B_283_1d3_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-283-1d3"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"r","text":"Except as otherwise provided in NRS 484B.287 [NRS-484B-287-1c, NRS-484B-287-1d, NRS-484B-287-1e, LVMC-11-30-060-A, LVMC-11-30-060-B], 484B.290 [LVMC-11-30-140-B] and 484B.350 [LVMC-11-46-030]:","role":"reference"},{"id":"c0","text":"Whenever signals exhibiting the words “Walk,” “Don’t Walk,” “Wait” or similar symbols are in place, such signals indicate as follows:","role":"condition"},{"id":"t","text":"While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated and flashing but is not accompanied by a countdown timer,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s1","text":"a pedestrian","role":"subject"},{"id":"ob1","text":"may not proceed to cross the highway,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s2","text":"but a pedestrian","role":"exception"},{"id":"e1","text":"who entered the highway lawfully pursuant to subparagraph (1)","role":"exception"},{"id":"ref2","text":"[NRS-484B-283-1d1]","role":"reference"},{"id":"e2","text":"may continue to cross the highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"ob2","text":"but must proceed to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone if one is provided or other place of safety before the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated and steady.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c0","atoms":["dev.pedestrian_signal","dev.governs","dev.position","kin.position","kin.heading","st.roadway","st.lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"Signals exhibiting 'Walk', 'Don't Walk', 'Wait' or similar symbols are pedestrian heads (dev.pedestrian_signal: 'a pedestrian head; state ∈ {walk, dont_walk_flashing, dont_walk_steady, dark}; countdown attribute'). The signal that indicates to a pedestrian ('such signals') is the head that governs the roadway or lane its crossing traverses (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls'