{"node_id":"NRS_484B_283_1d4_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-283-1d4"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"r","text":"Except as otherwise provided in NRS 484B.287 [NRS-484B-287-1c, NRS-484B-287-1d, NRS-484B-287-1e, LVMC-11-30-060-A, LVMC-11-30-060-B], 484B.290 [LVMC-11-30-140-B] and 484B.350 [LVMC-11-46-030]:","role":"reference"},{"id":"c0","text":"Whenever signals exhibiting the words “Walk,” “Don’t Walk,” “Wait” or similar symbols are in place, such signals indicate as follows:","role":"condition"},{"id":"t","text":"While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated and steady","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s1","text":"a pedestrian","role":"subject"},{"id":"ob1","text":"may not proceed to cross the highway,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s2","text":"but a pedestrian","role":"exception"},{"id":"e1","text":"who entered the highway lawfully pursuant to subparagraph (1) or (2)","role":"exception"},{"id":"ref2","text":"[NRS-484B-283-1d1, NRS-484B-283-1d2]","role":"reference"},{"id":"e2","text":"may continue to cross the highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"ob2","text":"but must proceed to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone if one is provided or other place of safety","role":"sibling"},{"id":"st","text":"as soon as possible.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"c0","atoms":["dev.pedestrian_signal","dev.governs","dev.position","kin.position","kin.heading","st.roadway","st.lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"Signals exhibiting 'Walk', 'Don't Walk', 'Wait' or similar symbols are pedestrian heads (dev.pedestrian_signal: 'a pedestrian head; state ∈ {walk, dont_walk_flashing, dont_walk_steady, dark}; countdown attribute'). The signal that indicates to a pedestrian is the head that governs the roadway or lane its crossing traverses (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls', traffic including pedestrians by DEF-NRS-484A-285; kinds st.roadway, st.lane) and that the pedestrian faces: dev.position ('location of the device head') ahead of kin.position along kin.heading ('direction the body points') within a cone and a reach. dev.position is not used as a stop line or crossing."},{"span":"t","atoms":["dev.pedestrian_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'illuminated and steady' is the head's state dont_walk_steady."},{"span":"s1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a pedestrian' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian."},{"span":"ob1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"Proceeding to cross the highway is coming onto the roadway or lane the head governs: the pedestrian's footprint comes to overlap it (rel.occupies of st.roadway / st.lane). The highway (DEF-NRS-484A-095) includes the sidewalk, but the sibling words 'must proceed to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone' place the sidewalk outside the crossing, so the crossing begins on the roadway."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a pedestrian' (the one excepted) is the same admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian."},{"span":"e1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.lane","st.sidewalk","dev.pedestrian_signal","dev.governs","dev.position","kin.position","kin.heading"],"derived":[],"source_spans":["ref2"],"justification":"Entering the highway lawfully pursuant to subparagraph (1) or (2) borrows their words: (1) 'While the “Walk” indication or walking person symbol is illuminated, pedestrians facing the signal may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal'; (2) 'While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated, is flashing and is accompanied by a countdown timer, a pedestrian may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal'. It is the pedestrian's latest step from a sidewalk (st.sidewalk) onto a roadway or lane (rel.occupies of st.roadway / st.lane) made while a pedestrian head (dev.pedestrian_signal) governing it (dev.governs) showed walk, or dont_walk_flashing with its countdown, and the pedestrian faced that head (dev.position ahead of kin.position along kin.heading within the cone and reach)."},{"span":"e2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"Continuing to cross is not having returned to a sidewalk (rel.occupies of st.sidewalk) since that entry."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"r","rule":"NRS_484B_287_1c","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"NRS_484B_287_1d","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"NRS_484B_287_1e","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_060_A","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_060_B","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_30_140_B_o2","map":{"subject":"subject"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_46_030_o1","map":{"subject":"v"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"r","rule":"LVMC_11_46_030_o2","map":{"subject":"v"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"ref2","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-283-1d1","quote":"While the “Walk” indication or walking person symbol is illuminated, pedestrians facing the signal may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal"},{"span":"ref2","as":"definition","source":"NRS-484B-283-1d2","quote":"While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated, is flashing and is accompanied by a countdown timer, a pedestrian may proceed across the highway in the direction of the signal"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"The subject is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian), not engaged by NRS_484B_287_1c, NRS_484B_287_1d, NRS_484B_287_1e, LVMC_11_30_060_A, LVMC_11_30_060_B, LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1 or LVMC_11_30_140_B_o2, with no vehicle v of the scene engaged by LVMC_11_46_030_o1 or LVMC_11_46_030_o2. There are a pedestrian head d (dev.pedestrian_signal) showing dont_walk_steady and a roadway or lane r governed by d (dev.governs), the subject faces d, and the subject's footprint did not overlap r at the previous observation. The subject faces d where, with Δ the vector from its kin.position to d's dev.position and h its kin.heading: h·Δ > 0, (h·Δ)² ≥ p.ped_signal_facing_cos² · (Δx² + Δy²), and Δx² + Δy² ≤ p.ped_signal_facing_reach². Excepted: the subject is continuing a crossing it began lawfully under subparagraph (1) or (2) — its latest step from a sidewalk onto a roadway or lane was made while a pedestrian head governing that roadway or lane showed walk, or dont_walk_flashing with its countdown, and the subject faced that head, and its footprint has overlapped no sidewalk since.","obligation":"The subject's footprint does not overlap r at this observation: it has not proceeded onto the roadway.","params":["p.ped_signal_facing_cos","p.ped_signal_facing_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"ob1","why":"'proceed to cross the highway' is read as the pedestrian's footprint coming onto the roadway or lane the faced head governs; walking on the sidewalk is not crossing.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"At the curb, the pedestrian faces a head 15 m away across roadway r that governs r and shows dont_walk_steady; at the next observation its footprint overlaps r."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same head and state; the pedestrian waits on the sidewalk."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The faced head shows walk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The pedestrian steps onto r facing the head, but the head's state is not observed.","masked":["dev.pedestrian_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The pedestrian stepped onto the first roadway while its head showed dont_walk_flashing with countdown, reached the median, and now steps onto the second roadway r while its faced head shows dont_walk_steady: it is continuing a lawful crossing."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.ped_signal_facing_cos","unit":"ratio","value":0.87,"convention":"cosine of the largest angle (about thirty degrees) between a pedestrian's heading and the line from its position to a pedestrian signal head at which the pedestrian counts as facing that head: the lateral offset of a far-side head from the crossing's line plus a pedestrian's heading wander","source":"MUTCD section 4E.08 (pedestrian signal heads placed at the far end of the crossing, in the pedestrian's line of sight)"},{"name":"p.ped_signal_facing_reach","unit":"m","value":40.0,"convention":"the largest distance from a pedestrian to a pedestrian signal head at which the head counts as the one across the crossing the pedestrian faces: a wide urban crossing (six lanes and a median, about 30 m) plus the head's set-back behind the far curb","source":"MUTCD section 4E.08; AASHTO Green Book urban cross-section widths"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_283_1d4_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-283-1d4"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"r","text":"Except as otherwise provided in NRS 484B.287 [NRS-484B-287-1c, NRS-484B-287-1d, NRS-484B-287-1e, LVMC-11-30-060-A, LVMC-11-30-060-B], 484B.290 [LVMC-11-30-140-B] and 484B.350 [LVMC-11-46-030]:","role":"reference"},{"id":"c0","text":"Whenever signals exhibiting the words “Walk,” “Don’t Walk,” “Wait” or similar symbols are in place, such signals indicate as follows:","role":"condition"},{"id":"t","text":"While the “Don’t Walk” or “Wait” indication or an upraised hand symbol is illuminated and steady","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s1","text":"a pedestrian","role":"sibling"},{"id":"ob1","text":"may not proceed to cross the highway,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s2","text":"but a pedestrian","role":"subject"},{"id":"e1","text":"who entered the highway lawfully pursuant to subparagraph (1) or (2)","role":"condition"},{"id":"ref2","text":"[NRS-484B-283-1d1, NRS-484B-283-1d2]","role":"reference"},{"id":"e2","text":"may continue to cross the highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"ob2","text":"but must proceed to a curb, sidewalk, safety zone if one is provided or other place of safety","role":"obligation"},{"id":"st","text":"as soon as possible.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"c0","atoms":["dev.pedestrian_signal","dev.governs","dev.position","kin.position","kin.heading","st.roadway","st.lane"],"derived":[],"justification":"Signals exhibiting 'Walk', 'Don't Walk', 'Wait' or similar symbols are pedestrian heads (dev.pedestrian_signal: 'a pedestrian head; state ∈ {walk, dont_walk_flashing, dont_walk_steady, dark}; countdown attribute'). The signal that indicates to a pedestrian is the head that governs the roadway or lane its crossing traverses (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls', traffic including pedestrians by DEF-NRS-484A-285; kinds st.roadway, st.lane) 